#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:5
msgid "The Linux exFAT filesystem driver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:16
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:18
msgid ""
"exFAT is a filesystem designed for removable storage and other devices that "
"need to store large files.  The Linux exFAT filesystem driver provides read "
"and write support for exFAT volumes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:22
msgid "To mount an exFAT volume, use the ``exfat`` filesystem type::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:28
msgid "Utilities support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:30
msgid ""
"The exfatprogs project provides userspace utilities for creating, checking, "
"repairing, inspecting, and tuning exFAT filesystems.  Use exfatprogs when "
"creating or checking an exFAT filesystem.  For example, use ``mkfs.exfat`` "
"to create a filesystem and ``fsck.exfat`` to check or repair one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:35
msgid "The project is available at:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:37
msgid "https://github.com/exfatprogs/exfatprogs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:41
msgid "Supported mount options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:43
msgid "The exFAT driver supports the following mount options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:46
msgid "uid="
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:47
msgid "gid="
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:47
msgid ""
"Set the owner and group of all files and directories.  The default is the "
"uid and gid of the process mounting the filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:51
msgid "umask="
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:51
msgid ""
"Set the permission mask for files and directories. The default is the umask "
"of the process mounting the filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:55
msgid "dmask="
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:55
msgid "Set the permission mask for directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:57
msgid "fmask="
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:57
msgid "Set the permission mask for files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:59
msgid "allow_utime="
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:59
msgid ""
"Control the permission check for changing file timestamps.  Only permission "
"bits 0022 are used. Permission bit 0020 allows members of the file's group "
"to change timestamps, and permission bit 0002 allows other users to change "
"timestamps.  The default is derived from dmask (``~dmask & 0022``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:66
msgid "iocharset=name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:66
msgid ""
"Character set used to convert between user-visible filenames and the UTF-16 "
"character encoding used by exFAT.  The default is "
"CONFIG_EXFAT_DEFAULT_IOCHARSET, which is ``utf8`` unless changed at kernel "
"configuration time.  Use ``iocharset=utf8`` for UTF-8 filename handling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:73
msgid "errors="
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:73
msgid ""
"Specify exFAT behavior on filesystem errors.  The value must be ``panic``, "
"``continue``, or ``remount-ro``.  These respectively panic, continue without "
"changing the filesystem, or remount the filesystem read-only.  The default "
"is ``remount-ro``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:80
msgid "discard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:80
msgid ""
"Issue discard/TRIM requests to the block device when clusters are freed.  "
"This is disabled by default.  ``nodiscard`` disables it explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:84
msgid "keep_last_dots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:84
msgid ""
"Keep trailing periods in path components during lookup.  Without this "
"option, trailing periods are stripped.  Existing entries with trailing "
"periods can be accessed when this option is enabled, but creating new "
"entries with trailing periods is rejected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:91
msgid "sys_tz"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:91
msgid ""
"Use the system timezone as the UTC offset when an exFAT timestamp does not "
"contain a valid timezone offset.  This takes precedence over time_offset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:95
msgid "time_offset=minutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:95
msgid ""
"Set the UTC offset, in minutes, used when an exFAT timestamp does not "
"contain a valid timezone offset. Values from -1440 to 1440 are accepted.  "
"The default is 0.  This option is ignored when sys_tz is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:100
msgid "zero_size_dir"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:100
msgid ""
"Create directories with zero size and without allocating a cluster.  This is "
"disabled by default; the default behavior allocates a cluster for a new "
"directory.  ``nozero_size_dir`` disables it explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:109
msgid "Deprecated mount options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:111
msgid ""
"The following options are accepted for compatibility but should not be used:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:113
msgid "``utf8``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:114
msgid "Deprecated.  Use ``iocharset=utf8`` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:116
msgid "``debug``, ``namecase=``, ``codepage=``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/exfat.rst:117
msgid "Deprecated and ignored by the exFAT driver."
msgstr ""
